{"step_index":222,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T21:00:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T02:30:57+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T02:31:01+05:30\nThe search for \"\"huihui-ai\" \"Qwen2.5-Coder-3B\" huggingface\" returned the following summary:\nThe user **huihui-ai** is a contributor on Hugging Face known for providing \"abliterated\" versions of various Large Language Models (LLMs)[1][2][3].\n\n### About the Model\nThe model **`huihui-ai/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct-abliterated`** is a fine-tuned, \"abliterated\" version of the official `Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct` model[2][4]. \n\n*   **Abliteration:** This process typically involves modifying the model's internal weights to remove or reduce the \"refusal\" behaviors often present in base instruction-tuned models, aiming to make them less prone to declining requests or giving \"AI assistant\" style refusals[5][6].\n*   **Base Architecture:** It is based on the Qwen2.5-Coder-3B series, which is a code-specific model developed by the Qwen team at Alibaba Cloud, designed for high-performance coding tasks[7][8].\n*   **Usage:** You can find this model and its derivatives (such as quantized versions for specific hardware) on Hugging Face[9][10].\n\n### Related Resources\n*   **Official Base Model:** [Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct)[4]\n*   **Hugging Face Profile:** You can browse all models contributed by [huihui-ai on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/huihui-ai) to see other abliterated variants[11][3].\n*   **Quantized Versions:** Because the model is popular in the local LLM community, third-party creators often provide GGUF or other quantized formats (e.g., for `llama.cpp` or mobile deployment) under their own namespaces, often referencing the `huihui-ai` original[10][12][13].\n\nSources:\n[1] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFkdtOSJSiO4386YLR61Pyd4UZx9xhYn