{"step_index":224,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T21:01:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T02:31:06+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T02:31:10+05:30\nThe search for \"\"unsloth/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct\" FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained unsloth colab\" returned the following summary:\nTo load the **Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct** model using Unsloth in a Google Colab environment, you should use the `FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained` method[1][2].\n\n### Basic Implementation\nYou can use the following code snippet to load the model and tokenizer. Unsloth is optimized for performance, so it is recommended to use `load_in_4bit=True` to save memory[3][2].\n\n```python\nfrom unsloth import FastLanguageModel\nimport torch\n\nmax_seq_length = 2048 # Supports RoPE Scaling internally\ndtype = None # None for auto detection\nload_in_4bit = True # Use 4bit quantization to reduce memory usage\n\nmodel, tokenizer = FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained(\n    model_name = \"unsloth/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct\",\n    max_seq_length = max_seq_length,\n    dtype = dtype,\n    load_in_4bit = load_in_4bit,\n)\n```\n\n### Key Considerations for Colab\n*   **Installation:** Ensure you have the latest version of Unsloth installed in your Colab environment[4]. You can install it using:\n    ```python\n    !pip install \"unsloth[colab-new] @ git+https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth.git\"\n    !pip install --no-deps \"xformers<0.0.27\" \"trl<0.9.0\" peft accelerate bitsandbytes\n    ```\n*   **Runtime:** Make sure your Colab runtime is set to **T4 GPU** (or better) via *Runtime > Change runtime type*[5][4].\n*   **Official Notebooks:** Unsloth provides dedicated, beginner-friendly Colab notebooks for Qwen 2.5 models[6][7]. You can find links to these notebooks in the [Unsloth Documentation](https://docs.unsloth.ai/) or their [GitHub repository](https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth)[8][9].\n*   **Performance:** The `from_pretrained` function automatically applies Unsloth's optimizations, making the model faster to load and memory-efficient compared to standard Hugging Face implementations[6][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.googl\n<truncated 174 bytes>\nnMZ73i0CW50OOdmEVWcoikRQnDu8sI7hRsqtMP3_8msHy9xWgvotKr0MIpCi5I9_By1TnZ9VzgavHlqd6TSGwc=)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGw09-SVtUEe5Lmb2iuoot6t5YYUxfH-R09zq_3u_QmURfTxhynDVyFS967ZxNNO2To6yAbt-dRxeeoGQ2swwJyW2i0rlT7iqSfRaxutteeocVEIxmdjA5Wvf6I1hJnOdQNTRdbhCNJRVPrcd_kUiuigwKRIGW7EbCRqS1P8rpGjpJ1LEmYK3YQ4F5GRM1EaQlVuMC8h5OH)\n[3] [kaggle.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGFezQql1MF94-tHBhiXLszqLChKQ2AIATNW7vjb-9f5QeO34ik1r01K4I51jPsNWuBT7BwxXl6JwxR-tNwYFupS_ra0TlH_aKdWc8nMC78R0AmwGuK-HsvczTTW44yl0AGAnN8QMh_Aev2PT9_uQvdc2cGxeEwqJykGtmaAHtxWQ==)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGOoQg_AyqdmnDsunu1C0A31TLiztKahMDrEE1dC4ZBVBfTA9OIGsZE58qcgq_ieuHD9f3IRLAwCGw0HSH6NH2byQK1OhakHz63Qx0Gu9SZc84zc2TW2aEKBENauC280oPfKt_meWHIFL-oG1qkvEBq4kPrdnQMSDCZMbR6gnm0yBIjvsrrwBUFJhY9XA==)\n[5] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGulCKOAGSxBDUJdTrfuNXDYU3PNLngiCrorEIcACqPyySlmXzr1z2HyOx0jkabVZvjjrwq0XLnmeIfMxPj-32Resl-ixkPV-u6F8VN3g6fUtF4j9iwmGY6BbPyKkPY-K8HpwOo9ap_xdDTCmDrVg==)\n[6] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG-iTocEj8KwMnhdIpSxtEU8rKSsPX9ry1VVRFsFKnfuV4RNJiB32W7A2j2pHdkhVlJs0pKGBaMz3X5x1vhMZDMLHIsCYNKl8IOeDRZgqhYFyhsQBKpuLdUyn6lHswEFVo79Gt48C9N_DPk5Lr59w==)\n[7] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHqhiErlZhLM6CGxzaH-MhCTEgxH3XoZ9OXMIQQjb6yU5BDajjozEtTOqi52H8MAlWc4Fj9ahp0oXe-ut1SlW6G9072ZjI1svF1smhtZ3c879aHbWSHvf1B)\n[8] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEyBtjnlO6u-1-0rVkDYcb7SD_aQ6y76sVbJX-pYskynRpBlRcSzITaBu7Oj62_Mf8yo